# Build-context exclusions for the images built from the REPOSITORY ROOT:
#   ingestion/Dockerfile            -> ingestion daemon
#   supabase/functions/Dockerfile   -> edge runtime (needs templates/physical-gateway)
#   tests/Dockerfile                -> conformance test runner
#
# ONE .dockerignore SERVES ALL THREE, so an exclusion added for one image can break another. That
# is not hypothetical: excluding `tests` for the ingestion build later broke the test-runner build,
# which needs tests/schemas -- and it failed as "/tests/schemas: not found" during COPY, which reads
# like a missing file rather than an ignored one.
#
# frontend/ has its own .dockerignore because it is built from its own context. It must keep
# frontend/src/utils/ -- the test runner reads sparkplugDatatype.js and model3d.js from THIS context
# for its drift checks against the edge worker's copies.

.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/coverage

# Local secrets. .env.example is deliberately NOT excluded -- it is the documented template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Nothing in these is read at build time by any of the three images; excluding them keeps the context
# small and, more importantly, stops an unrelated edit from busting the layer cache.
#
# `tests` is NOT excluded: tests/Dockerfile copies tests/schemas (the vendored IDTA metamodel schema)
# and it is 60 KB. Its absence would make the AAS suite skip its schema-conformance assertions -- the
# ones that caught three real metamodel violations -- while still reporting success.
#
# AND `docs/openapi.yaml` IS NOT EXCLUDED EITHER, which is the second time this file has caught
# somebody out in exactly the way its own header warns about. tests/Dockerfile:61 copies it --
# test_aas_api.py asserts that every route the service advertises is documented, so the spec is a
# FIXTURE of the suite and not only a deliverable. Without the negation the build fails as
# `"/docs/openapi.yaml": not found`, which reads like a deleted file rather than an ignored one.
#
# The negation has to come AFTER the `docs` line: Docker applies these in order and the last match
# wins. Putting it before makes it a no-op that looks correct.
docs
!docs/openapi.yaml
grafana
simulators
timescaledb
deploy
supabase/migrations/archive

*.md
!supabase/functions/**/*.md
